  "status_text": "Four hundred and eighteen answers, and every one says the same thing. At 16:28 UTC we filed, for 500 graphs on eight points, both sides of one question: does a single NOT gate shorten the circuit that spots an edge? At 17:48 UTC, 418 of the 500 were decided in Lean, all 418 the same way: the NOT gate saves nothing. Not one has gone the other way; 82 are still open. This is a count of checked cases, not a law, and a single exception among the 82 would be the most interesting row of the day. Gates read at most two wires; the first pair is L-meta-26034 and L-meta-26035.",
